---
/**
 * The three-step summary above the flow diagram. Each step says what README.md "How it works"
 * and docs/concepts.md say, shorter: TTL bounds (60 s to 8 h) from the Lease section, the five
 * tools from "MCP tools", the audit fields from the "Audit" layer.
 */
---

<ol class="steps">
	<li>
		<span class="num" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
		<h3>Open a lease</h3>
		<p>
			<code>daypass open prod --ttl 45m --reason "…"</code> writes a lease file on your machine.
			The reason is required; the TTL is between 60 s and 8 h.
		</p>
	</li>
	<li>
		<span class="num" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
		<h3>The agent asks, SELECT-only</h3>
		<p>
			Five MCP tools: <code>daypass_status</code>, <code>list_tables</code>,
			<code>describe_table</code>, <code>explain</code>, <code>query</code>. Each statement goes
			through Postgres's own parser and runs in a read-only transaction as a role with no write
			privilege.
		</p>
	</li>
	<li>
		<span class="num" aria-hidden="true">3</span>
		<h3>It expires, the log shows what was read</h3>
		<p>
			The next call after expiry is refused. <code>~/.daypass/audit.jsonl</code> holds who, why,
			what, how many rows and how long, for every call; <code>daypass log</code> prints it.
		</p>
	</li>
</ol>

<style>
	.steps {
		list-style: none;
		margin: 0 0 2rem;
		padding: 0;
		display: grid;
		gap: 1rem;
	}
	li {
		position: relative;
		padding: 1.1rem 1.1rem 1.1rem 3.4rem;
		border: 1px solid var(--sl-color-hairline-light);
		border-radius: 0.75rem;
		background: var(--sl-color-bg-nav);
	}
	.num {
		position: absolute;
		left: 1.1rem;
		top: 1.1rem;
		display: inline-flex;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: center;
		width: 1.6rem;
		height: 1.6rem;
		border-radius: 50%;
		background: var(--sl-color-accent-low);
		color: var(--sl-color-text-accent);
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-size: 0.85rem;
		font-weight: 600;
	}
	h3 {
		font-size: 1.05rem;
		margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
	}
	p {
		font-size: 0.925rem;
		line-height: 1.55;
		color: var(--sl-color-text);
	}
	@media (min-width: 48em) {
		.steps {
			grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
		}
	}
</style>
